"answer": "To improve balance and prevent falls, you should focus on balance exercises. Examples include tai chi, standing on one leg, or walking heel-to-toe [MLP-490][MLP-6603]. These activities improve stability and coordination, making it easier to walk on uneven surfaces and reducing fall risk [MLP-490][MLP-1530]. Additionally, strengthening your core muscles (abdomen, back, and hips) can further aid balance and stability [MLP-490]. Before starting, especially if you have trouble moving or balancing, consult your health care provider to ensure safety [MLP-490][MLP-6603]."
}
